de (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in SUMO2)"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":564,"end":564,"description":"Phosphothreonine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":576,"end":576,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":578,"end":578,"description":"Phosphothreonine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":626,"end":626,"description":"N6-acetyllysine; alternate"},{"type":"Cross-link","start":626,"end":626,"description":"Glycyl lysine isopeptide (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in ubiquitin); alternate"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":639,"end":639,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Region","start":656,"end":686,"description":"Interaction with RBBP4"},{"type":"Motif","start":696,"end":705,"description":"SH3-binding"},{"type":"Motif","start":711,"end":715,"description":"SUMO interaction motif 1 (SIM); crucial for efficient sumoylation"}],"interfaces":{},"subunit":[{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Component of the nucleosome remodeling and deacetylase (NuRD) repressor complex, composed of core proteins MTA1, MTA2, MTA3, RBBP4, RBBP7, HDAC1, HDAC2, MBD2, MBD3, and peripherally associated proteins CDK2AP1, CDK2AP2, GATAD2A, GATAD2B, CHD3, CHD4 and CHD5 (PubMed:16428440, PubMed:28977666, PubMed:33283408, PubMed:9885572). The exact stoichiometry of the NuRD complex is unknown, and some subunits such as MBD2 and MBD3, GATAD2A and GATAD2B, and CHD3, CHD4 and CHD5 define mutually exclusive NuRD complexes (PubMed:16428440, PubMed:28977666, PubMed:33283408). Interacts with RBBP4; the interaction is direct (PubMed:24920672). Interacts with BMAL1 (By similarity). Interacts with CLOCK (By similarity). Interacts with COP1 (PubMed:19805145). Interacts with CSNK1G2 in the cytoplasm (PubMed:15077195). Interacts with EP300 (PubMed:16617102). Interacts with HDAC2 (PubMed:17671180, PubMed:19805145, PubMed:21965678, PubMed:24970816). Interacts with IFI16 (PubMed:24413532). Interacts with ITGB3BP/CENPR (PubMed:15254226). Interacts with MBD3L2 (PubMed:15701600). Interacts with MDM2 (PubMed:19837670). Interacts with NACC2 (PubMed:22926524). Interacts with p53/TP53 (PubMed:19837670). Interacts with PIAS1 (PubMed:21965678). Interacts with PIAS3 (PubMed:21965678). Interacts with PIAS4 (PubMed:21965678). Interacts with PWWP2A (PubMed:30327463). Interacts with PWWP2B (By similarity). Interacts with SENP1 (PubMed:21965678). Interacts with SENP2 (PubMed:21965678). Interacts with SIX3; facilitates the binding of SIX3 to the core DNA motif of SIX3 promoter (PubMed:20682799). Interacts with SUMO1 (PubMed:21965678). Interacts with SUMO2 (PubMed:21965678). Interacts with TFCP2L1; which is indispensable for TFCP2L1-mediated self-renewal-promoting effect and endoderm-inhibiting action (By similarity). Interacts with TFAP2C (PubMed:24413532). Interacts with TPR (PubMed:24970816). Interacts with UBE2I/UBC9 (PubMed:21965678)"}],"isoforms":[{"accession":"Q13330-2","name":"Short","synonyms":["MTA1S"],"notes":[{"topic":"Function","text":"Binds to ESR1 and sequesters it in the cytoplasm and enhances its non-genomic responses"}],"length":430,"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000438610.5"],"refseq":["NM_001203258.2"],"refseqProteins":["NP_001190187.1"],"maneSelect":false,"decay":["ENST00000438610.5"],"onlyDecay":true},"segments":[[1,1,397]],"edits":[{"start":398,"end":715,"original":"TTQSYQWYSWGPPNMQCRLCASCWTYWKKYGGLKMPTRLD","replacement":"MSSLRILLDILEEIWWLENANPVRWREARTKPQ","added":33}],"missing":318,"replaced":0,"novel":33,"foldedAbsent":124,"foldedMissing":124,"features":[[5,23,0],[6,1,0],[7,1,0],[8,1,0],[9,1,0],[10,8,0],[11,1,0],[12,1,0],[13,1,0],[14,1,0],[15,1,0],[16,1,0],[17,1,0],[18,31,0],[19,10,0],[20,5,0]],"interfaces":{},"model":{"entry":"AF-Q13330-2-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-Q13330-2-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":81.1,"plddt":[[50,2],[70,2],[90,11],[70,6],[90,36],[70,1],[90,1],[70,5],[50,5],[0,1],[50,2],[0,2],[50,2],[0,6],[50,1],[0,1],[50,7],[70,10],[90,10],[70,1],[90,18],[70,9],[90,22],[70,2],[50,3],[70,13],[90,6],[70,